      "message": "I am not sure if its strictly necessary. Generic kernel code largely relies on cc_platform_has() API. cc_platform_set/clear APIs are used by platform/arch specific code to distinguish platforms within an arch (for ex: AMD/Intel). I also checked the (proposed) ARM64 CC implementation, which provides only cc_platform_has() API.\n\nhttps://patchwork.kernel.org/project/kvm/patch/20240701095505.165383-10-steven.price@arm.com/\n\nhttps://git.gitlab.arm.com/linux-arm/linux-cca.git cca-guest/v7\n\nI can add cc_platform_set/clear API if you still insist!",
